# Hexana CLI @VERSION@

This directory contains the native Hexana command-line products for the
supported release platforms.

Choose `hexana-cli` for `inspect-binary`, `summarize-binary`, `summarize-module`,
and `wasm-to-wat`. Choose `hexana-cli-script` for `run-script` and `test`. Choose
`hexana-wasm-tools` for `validate-and-explain`, `metadata-audit`, and
`component-wit-report`. All three products also provide `tools`, `version`,
and `help` and share this release version.

## Downloads

@DOWNLOADS_TABLE@

Each ZIP has a sibling `.sha256` file. Verify it before extracting:

```bash
shasum -a 256 -c hexana-cli-native-macos-arm64-@VERSION@.zip.sha256
unzip hexana-cli-native-macos-arm64-@VERSION@.zip
./bin/hexana-cli version
```

On Linux, use `sha256sum -c`. Every archive contains `LICENSE.txt` and
`THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md`. Machine-readable metadata is available in
[`hexana-cli-release-@VERSION@.json`](@DOWNLOADS_PREFIX@/hexana-cli-release-@VERSION@.json).
